# Markdown Source Format (MD)

`QuestionAsset.file_format='MD'` is the third source format alongside `IMG` and `DOC`. MD files are **self-contained**: LaTeX math via `$...$` / `$$...$$` and images embedded as `data:image/...;base64,...` URIs. **Single-slot only** — one `.md` per (question × asset_type × version); no `_PART` suffix, no part_number > 1.

## End-to-end pipeline

```
  ┌── ingest (filename ext .md/.markdown) ─────────┐
  ├── admin upload (.md, single-slot, size cap)    │
  ├── admin editor create/save (inline + fullscreen)──→ on disk in SOURCE_PATH
  └────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                          │
                          ├──→ render_file() (markdown-it-py + bleach)  ──→ dashboard cards / preview modal / viewer
                          │
                          └──→ _append_md_via_pandoc()  ──→ docx via pandoc subprocess + docxcompose
```

