## Locked decisions

1. **Self-contained MD**: no sidecar image files. Images MUST be base64 data URIs in the markdown source.
2. **Single-slot**: one MD per (question, asset_type, version). Multi-part is rejected at ingest (`upsert_asset`) and upload (`upload_question_asset`).
3. **Filename**: `<QID>_<VERSION>_<ATYPE>.md` (no `_PART` suffix). `VERSION` ∈ `EN/CH/BI/ENO/CHO`.
4. **Default format priority**: `IMG > MD > DOC` — but **user-configurable** at generation time via the Format Priority widget on the Generate page. Stored as `format_priority` comma list in `generation_options`.
5. **No server-side KaTeX**: math is left as `$...$` / `$$...$$` in HTML; the **client** (KaTeX auto-render) typesets it. The live editor's preview path runs `katex.renderToString()` client-side before marked because marked splits blank-line-separated `$$` into multiple `<p>` (breaks auto-render). Server render relies on dollarmath_plugin re-emitting delimiters.
6. **Editor stack**: EasyMDE + marked + KaTeX + FontAwesome 4.7 (pinned), all via CDN.

## Security model

**Threat surface**: admin-authored content rendered to other admins (and to read-only users on dashboard preview / viewer). Authors are trusted but compromised admin accounts are a concern.

[app/md_render.py](mdc:app/md_render.py) `sanitize()` enforces:
- **Tag allowlist** (`_ALLOWED_TAGS`): markdown-emitted tags + MathML elements + KaTeX-emitted `span/svg/path`. No `<script>`, `<iframe>`, `<object>`, etc.
- **Attribute callable** (`_attr_allowed`): per-tag attribute names + **URL scheme validation** via `_is_safe_url()`.
  - `<a href>`: only `http(s)`, `mailto`, `tel`, `/`, `#`, `//`. **Rejects `javascript:`, `vbscript:`, all `data:`**.
  - `<img src>`: same safe URLs, PLUS `data:image/<type>;base64,<...>` (the embedded-image case).
- **`protocols=_BLEACH_PROTOCOLS`** must include `data` — bleach pre-filters URL attributes against this list BEFORE invoking the callable. Without `data`, base64 images get silently stripped.
- `html: false` on the markdown-it instance — raw HTML in MD source is escaped, not parsed.
- `style` attribute is allowed (no CSS sanitizer); acceptable because authors are admins, not anonymous.

## Render cache

`render_file(asset_id, abs_path)`:
- Keyed by `asset_id → (mtime_ns, html)`.
- mtime read **BEFORE** content read so a concurrent writer can't desync the cached HTML from its mtime (otherwise next save's optimistic-mtime check would accept a stale write).
- LRU eviction at `_CACHE_MAX_ENTRIES = 512`.
- Invalidated on save (`save_md_asset_content`) and delete (`delete_question_asset` MD branch).
- Returns `''` on missing file or `UnicodeDecodeError` (corrupted UTF-8) — never caches errors.

## Admin endpoints

All require `@admin_required` + `_require_md_admin(question)` (subject-admin check).

| Method | URL | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| GET  | `/admin/questions/<qid>/assets/<aid>/md/content` | raw MD text + `mtime_ns` (**string** in JSON — ns precision) |
| POST | `/admin/questions/<qid>/assets/<aid>/md/save`    | overwrite file; body `{content, expected_mtime_ns?, force?}` (`expected_mtime_ns` string or int); **409 on optimistic conflict** |
| POST | `/admin/questions/<qid>/assets/md/create`        | new MD asset; body `{version, asset_type, content}` (legacy `language` accepted); **409 if slot already has MD** |
| GET  | `/admin/questions/<qid>/assets/<aid>/md/edit`    | fullscreen editor page |
| GET  | `/admin/questions/<qid>/assets/md/new?version=&asset_type=` | fullscreen editor in create mode (legacy `language=` accepted) |

Optimistic concurrency:
- `save` reads `expected_mtime_ns` from body; if disk mtime differs (and `force=False`), returns 409 with the current mtime. Editor prompts user to discard or force-overwrite.

## Editor (`templates/partials/md_editor.html`)

`oqbCreateMdEditor(textareaEl, {initialContent, maxSize, minHeight, onChange})` is the factory. Returns `{easymde, getValue, setValue, getBytes, getMaxBytes, focus, destroy}`.

Key behaviours:
- **Live preview pipeline**: `_oqbPreprocessMath()` runs KaTeX `renderToString()` for every `$...$` / `$$...$$` block first, then passes the resulting HTML through marked. This matches dashboard fidelity and survives blank-line-separated `$$` blocks. The inline regex **tolerates inner whitespace** (`$ D $` renders like `$D$`, captured trimmed) so legacy spaced math still previews; this is faithful to the docx because the server **tightens** `$ D $` → `$D$` before pandoc (see `normalize_inline_math` below). It still ignores currency-style `$5` via a "closing `$` not followed by a digit" guard.
- **Image insert / paste**: both produce `![](data:image/...;base64,...)` with **empty alt** (pandoc would otherwise render alt as a visible caption in the docx).
- **Paste isolation**: CodeMirror paste handler calls `e.stopPropagation()` so the outer admin-page document-level paste handler doesn't ALSO upload the image as an IMG asset. [templates/admin_questions.html](mdc:templates/admin_questions.html) also defensively skips its paste handler when the MD modal is showing or focus is inside an `.EasyMDEContainer`.
- **Fullscreen reparenting**: a MutationObserver watches for EasyMDE's `.fullscreen` class. On entry, the entire `.EasyMDEContainer` is physically moved to `<body>` (placeholder left behind in the original spot), bypassing the Bootstrap-modal stacking-context trap that would otherwise confine the `position: fixed` editor inside the modal. On exit it's restored. `destroy()` exits fullscreen first so the textarea isn't reparented onto `<body>`.
- **Toolbar collision**: `button.table` is scoped via `.EasyMDEContainer .editor-toolbar button.table { width: auto !important; }` because Bootstrap's `.table { width: 100% }` otherwise stretches the Insert-Table button to the full toolbar.
- **Idempotent include**: script body bails immediately if `window.oqbCreateMdEditor` is already defined.

## Generation (`_append_md_via_pandoc`)

```
md file → _preprocess_md_for_pandoc → tmp/input.md →
   pandoc --from=markdown+tex_math_dollars+tex_math_double_backslash-implicit_figures → tmp/fragment.docx →
   docxcompose.Composer(master).append(fragment)
```

Why each piece matters:
- **`_preprocess_md_for_pandoc`**: (1) collapses blank lines INSIDE `$$...$$` blocks — pandoc's `tex_math_dollars` treats blank lines as paragraph breaks, so `$$\n\nformula\n\n$$` becomes three paragraphs and the math never renders; (2) calls `ai_prompts.normalize_inline_math` to **tighten padded inline math** (`$ x $` → `$x$`). `tex_math_dollars` only recognises inline math with no space right inside the `$`, so spaced delimiters render as literal text in the docx; tightening here fixes legacy/AI-generated files in place. AI-generated MD is *also* tightened at write time (`ai_tools.generate_md_slot` calls `normalize_inline_math`) and the MD prompt asks for tight `$x$`, escaped question numbers (`8\.`), and one MC option per line.
- **`-implicit_figures`**: disabled so a standalone `![](data:...)` image is rendered as a plain inline image, NOT a captioned figure with the alt text shown below.
- **`tex_math_dollars+tex_math_double_backslash`**: enable `$...$` and `$$...$$` parsing AND allow `\\` line breaks in math.
- **Pandoc resolution**: `_append_md_via_pandoc` falls back to standard Windows install paths (`C:\Program Files\Pandoc\pandoc.exe` etc.) when `shutil.which('pandoc')` fails — installers update PATH only for *new* shells, so a freshly-installed pandoc is invisible to long-running Flask processes.
- **Format order in generation**: `add_question_content_to_doc` takes a `format_priority` arg (defaults to `_DEFAULT_FORMAT_PRIORITY = ('IMG','MD','DOC')`) threaded from `create_word_document` and ultimately from the form `format_priority`.

## DOC pipeline lives elsewhere
The MD pipeline is independent of the DOC pipeline. DOC source files go through Microsoft Word COM (`app/word_com.py`), not pandoc / docxcompose. The two coexist inside `add_question_content_to_doc` as separate format branches. See [docx-source-format.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/docx-source-format.mdc) for the DOC pipeline.

## Common gotchas (read me before changing things)

1. **DO NOT** add raw markdown processing to the live preview without preserving the KaTeX preprocess step. marked + auto-render alone breaks on blank-line-separated `$$...$$`.
2. **DO NOT** drop `data` from `_BLEACH_PROTOCOLS` — base64 images will silently disappear. The narrow gate is in `_attr_allowed`, not the protocol list.
3. **DO NOT** call `easymde.toTextArea()` while the editor is in fullscreen mode without first calling `toggleFullScreen()` — the container has been reparented to `<body>` and the textarea would end up there too.
4. **DO NOT** use `easymde.maxHeight` option in modal contexts — it collapses the side-by-side preview to ~77px. Bound heights with CSS instead.
5. **DO NOT** assume `data-preview-version` defaults work — `oqbLoadMarkdownPreviewCards` reads `data-preview-version` (falling back to legacy `data-preview-lang`), and admin cards explicitly set it per (version × atype) slot.
6. **DO** invalidate `md_render` cache on every disk write to MD files (save, delete). The mtime check is the safety net but eager invalidation gives more deterministic behaviour, especially across processes.
7. **DO** keep `viewer.html` helpers (`oqbTypesetMath`, `oqbRenderMarkdownInto`) in sync with `base.html` — viewer.html does NOT extend base.html.
8. **DO** keep the reorder endpoint and frontend `moveAssetPart` IMG-only — MD and DOC are single-slot.

## Pandoc external dependency

Required for document generation. **Not** a pip package. Install separately:
- Windows: https://github.com/jgm/pandoc/releases (or `winget install --id=JohnMacFarlane.Pandoc`)
- Linux: `apt install pandoc` or distro equivalent
- macOS: `brew install pandoc`

If not on PATH, set `PANDOC_PATH=<full path to binary>` in `.env`. On Windows the resolver also checks `C:\Program Files\Pandoc\pandoc.exe` and a few standard locations as fallback.

Without pandoc, MD assets in generated docx fall through to italic placeholder text — generation does NOT fail entirely.
